{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm","id":980034,"title":"Metis and the Defiler Wyrm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-01T20:20:00-07:00","id":980034,"title":"Metis and the Defiler Wyrm","content":"So I'm rereading the corebook in preparation for my first time running Werewolf the Apocalypse, first time playing it in 13 years, and I got to the section on Rage and how a wyrm tainted rage can result. Specifically the Metis curse upsets most of my players, to the point where even a fade to black isn't satisfactory. This in mind, I've come up with a replacement Thrall of the Wyrm result whenever it comes up for Metis. I wanted to present this here in case it's too 'out there'.<br /> <br /> <b>Metis</b>: The Defiler Wyrm reserves special attention for those Garou who cannot breed themselves. In the Thrall of the Wyrm, a bizarre form of empathy occurs. The Defiler Wyrm understands that yearning, the need to create, but the Defiler Wyrm cannot create like the Wyld can, it can only destroy or pervert. So it is with the metis breed. If a werewolf kills or incapacitates an opponent, her player must roll Wits (difficulty 7). If the roll botches, the werewolf's connection to the Defiler Wyrm imparts a profane secret - the ability to twist the hearts and souls of others into a likeness of their own tortured selves. If the victim survives, they become a twisted mockery of a the garou, a werewolf not unlike the false myths held true by the herd. If the victim dies, their spirit becomes corrupted and terrible. Either way, the metis can't help but sense the kinship that exists between themselves and their creation, forced to realize with guilt the truth that they have created a being of sin, much as their parents did to them. The feeling of kinship extends both ways - at first, most living victims are horrified by what is happening to them, after the first few transformations, the corruption sets in, and they can't imagine themselves without it. One way or another the metis is forced to deal with the consequences of their own creation, and the 'child' is likely to play games with them as they sink deeper into wyrm-tainted corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:37:28-07:00","id":980069,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd like to get rid of most of the concept of Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies altogether. It takes something away from debate positions on the nature of Rage, and it has a forced correspondence that doesn't hold up as some kind of map to who's closer to which Triatic Wyrm, by breed. I'd rather just have them be irresistible frenzies with a touch of the lupus or homid problems, depending on the context of the frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:35:20-07:00","id":980104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980069#post980069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd like to get rid of most of the concept of Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies altogether. It takes something away from debate positions on the nature of Rage, and it has a forced correspondence that doesn't hold up as some kind of map to who's closer to which Triatic Wyrm, by breed. I'd rather just have them be irresistible frenzies with a touch of the lupus or homid problems, depending on the context of the frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done this before, and for as rare as they (thrall frenzies) are it doesn't seem to take anything away from the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T01:06:40-07:00","id":980151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980069#post980069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd like to get rid of most of the concept of Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies altogether. It takes something away from debate positions on the nature of Rage, and it has a forced correspondence that doesn't hold up as some kind of map to who's closer to which Triatic Wyrm, by breed. I'd rather just have them be irresistible frenzies with a touch of the lupus or homid problems, depending on the context of the frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and given what the metis thrall is, I rather not have it in the game. Dark the setting might be, but you should never leave it to the dice whether a pc rapes another character, pc or npc. If rape is to be used in-game by or to a PC, it should be agreed upon by the group. Because you don't know if anyone has trauma surrounding it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T07:03:18-07:00","id":980226,"title":"","content":"You are only going to go into the Thrall of the Wyrm if you score 6 successes on a Rage roll and you only commit you atrocity if you botch a Wits roll when facing your trigger (a dead ir incapacitated foe while suffering the Thrall of the Wyrm). To suffer from the Metis Thrall of the Wyrm you have to a) be Garou, b) have a Rage 6+, and c) be Metis. If you do not want to have a chance to suffer it, do not be one of those three things.<br /> <br /> While everyone has the right to modify canon to their heart's desire for their games, the Thrall of the Wyrm represents the seed of corruption within each Garou. It is the price associated for having Rage 6+, so people who are uncomfortable with it should not develop high levels of Rage. Alternatively, you should develop high levels of Wits, to reduce the probability of botching the roll when the trigger occurs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T07:11:09-07:00","id":980230,"title":"","content":"The question to be asked is whether there's more utility created for the game - and by the game, I mean the following: The setting, the mechanics, the players, and the stories those three things in combination create, with the weight being given to the latter two components - to include, as a core rule, mandatory random-chance based sexual assault than the alternative, which would be to not include a core rule mechanic dealing with a very sensitive issue.<br /> <br /> I can't see any reasonable argument why the manifestation of the thrall of the wyrm must be a mandatory sexual assault in the case of metis, when there are numerous other options that could be used without reducing the danger of the thrall of the wyrm, it's impact, and its potential for pathos. I thus fail to see why there is more utility to be gained in including the rule as written than there is in altering or omitting it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T07:52:16-07:00","id":980237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980226#post980226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are only going to go into the Thrall of the Wyrm if you score 6 successes on a Rage roll and you only commit you atrocity if you botch a Wits roll when facing your trigger (a dead ir incapacitated foe while suffering the Thrall of the Wyrm). To suffer from the Metis Thrall of the Wyrm you have to a) be Garou, b) have a Rage 6+, and c) be Metis. If you do not want to have a chance to suffer it, do not be one of those three things.<br /> <br /> While everyone has the right to modify canon to their heart's desire for their games, the Thrall of the Wyrm represents the seed of corruption within each Garou. It is the price associated for having Rage 6+, so people who are uncomfortable with it should not develop high levels of Rage. Alternatively, you should develop high levels of Wits, to reduce the probability of botching the roll when the trigger occurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>All technically true, and all irrelevant for what we're talking about. Once you get to the point of hacking the game, textual-level details setting up the original state don't matter anymore. Everything can be changed, like reflective surfaces no longer being absolutely required to step sideways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:31:16-07:00","id":980255,"title":"","content":"So for context (from my part): In a Werewolf game I played in where we played every weekend for 2 years straight, and the follow up/continuation of that game for another year and a half (3 1/2 years total game time, every week; over 150 sessions) Thrall came up 2, maybe 3 times. And only once did a played botch their Wits role (they were Lupus) and really, it didn't add <i>anything</i> to the story.<br /> <br /> If a mechanic literally adds nothing to the story, it doesn't make a difference if you drop it entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980226#post980226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are only going to go into the Thrall of the Wyrm if you score 6 successes on a Rage roll and you only commit you atrocity if you botch a Wits roll when facing your trigger (a dead ir incapacitated foe while suffering the Thrall of the Wyrm). To suffer from the Metis Thrall of the Wyrm you have to a) be Garou, b) have a Rage 6+, and c) be Metis. If you do not want to have a chance to suffer it, do not be one of those three things.<br /> <br /> While everyone has the right to modify canon to their heart's desire for their games, the Thrall of the Wyrm represents the seed of corruption within each Garou. It is the price associated for having Rage 6+, so people who are uncomfortable with it should not develop high levels of Rage. Alternatively, you should develop high levels of Wits, to reduce the probability of botching the roll when the trigger occurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This thread is about changing the rules because players are uncomfortable with the Rules as Written. Explaining why they shouldn't want to is unhelpful at best.<br /> <br /> Also, want prices associated with high Rage that aren't Thrall?<br /> The Curse is the first one that comes to mind. 6+ Rage affects over 75% of the population. The interaction between Rage and Gnosis and possibly attacking packmates in Frenzy is another. The possibility of attacking friends and allies while in Frenzy is another. There are plenty of (more common) way to represent the supposed &quot;seed of corruption within each Garou&quot; without having players <u>have to</u> sexually assault each other (even if it's only a minute chance of happening).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:51:39-07:00","id":980261,"title":"","content":"Since when do player's have to sexually attack players? Unless they changed it in W20, the exact line in Revised (Core, p. 191) is 'if a metis kills or incapacitates a foe while in the Thrall'. It is the other two forms of Thrall that say opponent (friend or foe), but the metis Thrall specifically mentions foe rather than opponent (friend or foe) in the text and the rule. If any ST forced a metis to sexually assault a fallen friend, they were in the wrong and should apologize to their players.<br /> <br /> Of course you should change a rule that you are uncomfortable with, but there is something to be said about the responsibilities of the players and the STs. It is the player who chooses to gain Rage 6+ and it is the player who chooses to play a metis, so it is the player's responsibility when they create a circumstance that, according to the rules, would lead to the Metis Thrall (it is also the ST who is responsible for allowing such a character if they are worried that such an event will traumatize the table). If players are uncomfortable with the Metis Thrall rules, they should not acquire Rage 6+ or they should not play a metis (if STs are uncomfortable with the Metis Thrall rules, they should not allow any characters that would trigger those rules). As an ST, I never allowed players to create metis Garou characters for exactly that reason (and because it allowed me to show the victimization of the metis in Garou society without having to victimize any players).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:56:08-07:00","id":980265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980255#post980255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This thread is about changing the rules because players are uncomfortable with the Rules as Written. Explaining why they shouldn't want to is unhelpful at best.<br /> <br /> Also, want prices associated with high Rage that aren't Thrall?<br /> The Curse is the first one that comes to mind. 6+ Rage affects over 75% of the population. The interaction between Rage and Gnosis and possibly attacking packmates in Frenzy is another. The possibility of attacking friends and allies while in Frenzy is another. There are plenty of (more common) way to represent the supposed &quot;seed of corruption within each Garou&quot; without having players <u>have to</u> sexually assault each other (even if it's only a minute chance of happening).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, rage 6+ is essentially saying goodbye to any sort of normal life. And it can be devastating once the PC realises what that means. That, and you become a liability to the pack, get angry too easily and not being able to act subtly. As much as garou see frenzy as part of them, one prone to it won't be seen worth giving high rank to or trusted to do anything above being a living shredder.<br /> <br /> Then there is the second fact, RPs are safe places and continue to be even if you play WoD. Stuff like rape in the background or victims of rape aren't the issue here. It is that one of the PCs, due to a bad roll, has to rape someone on-screen. Unless this has been discussed and agreed upon by -all- players, it can come off as too excessive or hurt someone. And justifying it by stating that WoD is dark and bad things happen to me just reads callous towards other players and their limits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:00:00-07:00","id":980268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980261#post980261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when do player's have to sexually attack players? Unless they changed it in W20, the exact line in Revised (Core, p. 191) is 'if a metis kills or incapacitates a foe while in the Thrall'. It is the other two forms of Thrall that say opponent (friend or foe), but the metis Thrall specifically mentions foe rather than opponent (friend or foe) in the text and the rule. If any ST forced a metis to sexually assault a fallen friend, they were in the wrong and should apologize to their players.<br /> <br /> Of course you should change a rule that you are uncomfortable with, but there is something to be said about the responsibilities of the players and the STs. It is the player who chooses to gain Rage 6+ and it is the player who chooses to play a metis, so it is the player's responsibility when they create a circumstance that, according to the rules, would lead to the Metis Thrall (it is also the ST who is responsible for allowing such a character if they are worried that such an event will traumatize the table). If players are uncomfortable with the Metis Thrall rules, they should not acquire Rage 6+ or they should not play a metis (if STs are uncomfortable with the Metis Thrall rules, they should not allow any characters that would trigger those rules). As an ST, I never allowed players to create metis Garou characters for exactly that reason (and because it allowed me to show the victimization of the metis in Garou society without having to victimize any players).</div> </div> </div> </div>I put it to you that a mechanic requiring <i>any</i> form of sexual assault by or against the players to take place for the rules as written to function is unnecessary. Do you disagree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:11:29-07:00","id":980273,"title":"","content":"Yes, I disagree, because the rules are obviously designed to punish munchkin behavior (and are designed to illustrate the inhuman anger of characters with Rage 6+). If the players choose to take advantage of the game mechanics that would lead to that form of punishment and then whine about it when their munchkin behavior bites them in their rear ends, it is the fault of the players. They might as well whine about how unfair it is that they will likely die when they jump off of a skyscraper to avoid a fight that they instigated (yes, I have had players do that and, no, they did not get to survive unless they were Dhampyr).<br /> <br /> There are two simple solutions to this problem, a) don't take Rage 6+ or b) don't play a Metis. If an ST is uncomfortable with the rule, like I am, then they should ban Metis player characters in the games, like I have in my games. If a PC is uncomfortable with the rule, like most people seem to be, then they should either a) not take Rage 6+ or b) not play a Metis. Alternatively, the ST should roll the Wits dice for the players in secret, and lie about the results when they do botch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:43:50-07:00","id":980303,"title":"","content":"Why, then, is the necessary means of punishing munchkin behaviour - which I do not necessarily accept that such a character must necessarily exhibit - a sexual assault scene? What does this contribute that an alternative Thrall state cannot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:20:54-07:00","id":980317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980273#post980273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They might as well whine about how unfair it is that they will likely die when they jump off of a skyscraper to avoid a fight that they instigated (yes, I have had players do that and, no, they did not get to survive unless they were Dhampyr).</div> </div> </div> </div> Surviving 10 levels of Agg (which you take from that fall) is easy enough for a Crinos Garou, but that is completely besides the point here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980273#post980273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There are two simple solutions to this problem, a) don't take Rage 6+ or b) don't play a Metis. If an ST is uncomfortable with the rule, like I am, then they should ban Metis player characters in the games, like I have in my games. If a PC is uncomfortable with the rule, like most people seem to be, then they should either a) not take Rage 6+ or b) not play a Metis.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or and even easier third solution: you can just not use the rule that everyone (Players and STs, according to you) is uncomfortable with. It in no way punishes munchkin behavior (that doesn't already come up more often according to other rules in the game).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980273#post980273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, the ST should roll the Wits dice for the players in secret, and lie about the results when they do botch.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are going to roll in secret and lie about the result, then don't have the roll to begin with. Period. There is absolutely no point in rolling something if the outcome is already decided.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T10:26:41-07:00","id":980320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm#post980034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm rereading the corebook in preparation for my first time running Werewolf the Apocalypse, first time playing it in 13 years, and I got to the section on Rage and how a wyrm tainted rage can result. Specifically the Metis curse upsets most of my players, to the point where even a fade to black isn't satisfactory. This in mind, I've come up with a replacement Thrall of the Wyrm result whenever it comes up for Metis. I wanted to present this here in case it's too 'out there'.<br /> <br /> <b>Metis</b>: The Defiler Wyrm reserves special attention for those Garou who cannot breed themselves. In the Thrall of the Wyrm, a bizarre form of empathy occurs. The Defiler Wyrm understands that yearning, the need to create, but the Defiler Wyrm cannot create like the Wyld can, it can only destroy or pervert. So it is with the metis breed. If a werewolf kills or incapacitates an opponent, her player must roll Wits (difficulty 7). If the roll botches, the werewolf's connection to the Defiler Wyrm imparts a profane secret - the ability to twist the hearts and souls of others into a likeness of their own tortured selves. If the victim survives, they become a twisted mockery of a the garou, a werewolf not unlike the false myths held true by the herd. If the victim dies, their spirit becomes corrupted and terrible. Either way, the metis can't help but sense the kinship that exists between themselves and their creation, forced to realize with guilt the truth that they have created a being of sin, much as their parents did to them. The feeling of kinship extends both ways - at first, most living victims are horrified by what is happening to them, after the first few transformations, the corruption sets in, and they can't imagine themselves without it. One way or another the metis is forced to deal with the consequences of their own creation, and the 'child' is likely to play games with them as they sink deeper into wyrm-tainted corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shying away from the tangent this spawned and back on the initial topic.<br /> I think that mechanic is interesting, but goes against the general idea of how Thrall works. Thrall is supposed to be a personal<br /> effect. In the proposed system, the Metis Garou's Thrall consequences are put on the victim instead of affecting themselves. I don't know that I would allow a character's personal Thrall to change the victim on a supernatural level. It just seems off to me and I might be having a hard time explaining why (lack of sleep is fun).<br /> <br /> Like I said, I do think it's a cool mechanic. I could see it being a curse of some type laid upon a character by an outside force, and it would make for an interesting story. I just don't think it should be something laid into the groundwork of the game rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T13:27:56-07:00","id":980401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980273#post980273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I disagree, because the rules are obviously designed to punish munchkin behavior (and are designed to illustrate the inhuman anger of characters with Rage 6+). If the players choose to take advantage of the game mechanics that would lead to that form of punishment and then whine about it when their munchkin behavior bites them in their rear ends, it is the fault of the players. They might as well whine about how unfair it is that they will likely die when they jump off of a skyscraper to avoid a fight that they instigated (yes, I have had players do that and, no, they did not get to survive unless they were Dhampyr).<br /> <br /> There are two simple solutions to this problem, a) don't take Rage 6+ or b) don't play a Metis. If an ST is uncomfortable with the rule, like I am, then they should ban Metis player characters in the games, like I have in my games. If a PC is uncomfortable with the rule, like most people seem to be, then they should either a) not take Rage 6+ or b) not play a Metis. Alternatively, the ST should roll the Wits dice for the players in secret, and lie about the results when they do botch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the developers created the Thrall of the Wyrm for the sake of punishing munchkin behavior then they must have been pretty ignorant. You don't punish munchkin behaviors by brutally attacking a person emotionally, you do it by making it a mechanical inconvenience to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T13:30:30-07:00","id":980404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980320#post980320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shying away from the tangent this spawned and back on the initial topic.<br /> I think that mechanic is interesting, but goes against the general idea of how Thrall works. Thrall is supposed to be a personal<br /> effect. In the proposed system, the Metis Garou's Thrall consequences are put on the victim instead of affecting themselves. I don't know that I would allow a character's personal Thrall to change the victim on a supernatural level. It just seems off to me and I might be having a hard time explaining why (lack of sleep is fun).<br /> <br /> Like I said, I do think it's a cool mechanic. I could see it being a curse of some type laid upon a character by an outside force, and it would make for an interesting story. I just don't think it should be something laid into the groundwork of the game rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the input, and for actually constructively reviewing the proposed mechanic~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:12:28-07:00","id":980725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980401#post980401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the developers created the Thrall of the Wyrm for the sake of punishing munchkin behavior then they must have been pretty ignorant. You don't punish munchkin behaviors by brutally attacking a person emotionally, you do it by making it a mechanical inconvenience to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thrall of the Wyrm is really mechanically inconvenient when it goes off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:54:34-07:00","id":980887,"title":"","content":"And why is the Metis Thrall so much worse that the Homids or Lupus Thrall? Is cannibalizing or murdering you incapacitated friends that much better than raping your foes? While rape is a horrible thing, your foes have a better chance of surviving the Metis Thrall than the Homids or Lupus Thrall, and you do not have to worry about attacking your friends with the Metis Thrall.<br /> <br /> If you do not want to deal with the Thrall of the Wyrm, just tell your players that any character tbat develops Rage 6+ becomes an NPC because they are too uncontrollable for normal Garou society. Or you could house rule that Thrall of the Wyrm only manifests when Rage exceeds the greater of Gnosis or Willpower. I would, however, keep the Thrall of the Wyrm as a rule, to represent the dangers of extreme Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:57:59-07:00","id":980889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980887#post980887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why is the Metis Thrall so much worse that the Homids or Lupus Thrall? Is cannibalizing or murdering you incapacitated friends that much better than raping your foes? While rape is a horrible thing, your foes have a better chance of surviving the Metis Thrall than the Homids or Lupus Thrall, and you do not have to worry about attacking your friends with the Metis Thrall.<br /> <br /> If you do not want to deal with the Thrall of the Wyrm, just tell your players that any character tbat develops Rage 6+ becomes an NPC because they are too uncontrollable for normal Garou society. Or you could house rule that Thrall of the Wyrm only manifests when Rage exceeds the greater of Gnosis or Willpower. I would, however, keep the Thrall of the Wyrm as a rule, to represent the dangers of extreme Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because rape is an exceptionally sensitive subject, above and beyond killing and cannibalism in many cases. Also, you do have to worry about attacking your friends in Metis thrall, but that isn't the problem. The problem is rape-as-mechanical-penalty in the first place.<br /> <br /> I ask you again, since you neglected to actually answer. Why should it be a sexual assault scene? What does this contribute that an alternative Thrall state cannot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:24:10-07:00","id":980904,"title":"","content":"What does a cannibalism scene involving the victimization of a friend contribute? What does a murder scene involving the victimization of a friend contribute? If you think that it is that sensitive of a subject, fade to black (I would really suggest fading to black during any Thrall moment anyway) and, when the frenzy ends, have the character coming to beside the abused body (or corpse) of their victim. The PC and the ST are explicitly wanting to deal with the Thrall of the Wyrm when they choose to make a character with Rage 6+, it is not an esoteric rule because it is in the Core (Revised), so it is their responsibility for making (or allowing) a character that would fall to the Thrall of the Wyrm. <br /> <br /> For an alternative Thrall to make sense, it would have to be as horrific as the other forms of Thrall. The Thrall of the Wyrm focuses on the three major taboos of Western society (Homid=Cannibalism, Metis=Rape, and Lupus=Murder). The question for the creation of an alternate Thrall rule is what would be an appropriate replacement taboo (the incest taboo is covered with the creation of the Metis and would not be appropriate for a frenzy situation anyway). I really cannot imagine an appropriate taboo that would replace the rape taboo associated with the Metis Thrall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:48:16-07:00","id":980916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980904#post980904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For an alternative Thrall to make sense, it would have to be as horrific as the other forms of Thrall. The Thrall of the Wyrm focuses on the three major taboos of Western society (Homid=Cannibalism, Metis=Rape, and Lupus=Murder). The question for the creation of an alternate Thrall rule is what would be an appropriate replacement taboo (the incest taboo is covered with the creation of the Metis and would not be appropriate for a frenzy situation anyway). I really cannot imagine an appropriate taboo that would replace the rape taboo associated with the Metis Thrall.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the lupus one isn't exactly the best thought one, either. I mean, you are literally using the very peak of human capability of strength <i>at minium</i>, you are essentially the flash by the speed of your actions with Rage, and your weapons are fangs and claws. That opponent is going to end up looking like chunky salsa whether regular fight, frenzy or thrall.<br /> <br /> As to why rape stands out over cannibalism, there are few reasons.<br /> <br /> While being eaten alive -would- be extremely traumatic, we don't tend to munch on each other very often these days. At most, you will run into people who have been eaten by animals, rather than other people. It is simply not a very common trauma. Rape, on the other hand, is sadly very common. Not only that, but the dynamic is not of hunger and feeding, but of domination over another and their body.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that the act of eating -itself- is not the issue, it is the meat. And even then, the focus is on you as a lunch. Rape is forcing someone to be violated, and usually the thing it hurts most is you as a person, rather than your body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:34:24-07:00","id":980945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm#post980034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm rereading the corebook in preparation for my first time running Werewolf the Apocalypse, first time playing it in 13 years, and I got to the section on Rage and how a wyrm tainted rage can result. Specifically the Metis curse upsets most of my players, to the point where even a fade to black isn't satisfactory. This in mind, I've come up with a replacement Thrall of the Wyrm result whenever it comes up for Metis. I wanted to present this here in case it's too 'out there'.<br /> <br /> <b>Metis</b>: The Defiler Wyrm reserves special attention for those Garou who cannot breed themselves. In the Thrall of the Wyrm, a bizarre form of empathy occurs. The Defiler Wyrm understands that yearning, the need to create, but the Defiler Wyrm cannot create like the Wyld can, it can only destroy or pervert. So it is with the metis breed. If a werewolf kills or incapacitates an opponent, her player must roll Wits (difficulty 7). If the roll botches, the werewolf's connection to the Defiler Wyrm imparts a profane secret - the ability to twist the hearts and souls of others into a likeness of their own tortured selves. If the victim survives, they become a twisted mockery of a the garou, a werewolf not unlike the false myths held true by the herd. If the victim dies, their spirit becomes corrupted and terrible. Either way, the metis can't help but sense the kinship that exists between themselves and their creation, forced to realize with guilt the truth that they have created a being of sin, much as their parents did to them. The feeling of kinship extends both ways - at first, most living victims are horrified by what is happening to them, after the first few transformations, the corruption sets in, and they can't imagine themselves without it. One way or another the metis is forced to deal with the consequences of their own creation, and the 'child' is likely to play games with them as they sink deeper into wyrm-tainted corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lovely defiling, and far more appropriate than bizarre sex acts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:41:27-07:00","id":980948,"title":"","content":"I could see torture as a replacement. It's taboo, and suitably wyrmish. Not simply defeating your foe, but leaving them with permanent (barring regeneration) injuries and reminders. Cutting off thumbs, leaving the face a mass of scars, destroying eyes, hobbling legs, etc... Something over the top and cruel that doesn't leave people impressed with your skill, but wondering what is wrong with you to do something so monstrous. It also works for the Metis, turning the torment they've experienced outwards, making the world hurt the way they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:37:28-07:00","id":980988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980948#post980948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see torture as a replacement. It's taboo, and suitably wyrmish. Not simply defeating your foe, but leaving them with permanent (barring regeneration) injuries and reminders. Cutting off thumbs, leaving the face a mass of scars, destroying eyes, hobbling legs, etc... Something over the top and cruel that doesn't leave people impressed with your skill, but wondering what is wrong with you to do something so monstrous. It also works for the Metis, turning the torment they've experienced outwards, making the world hurt the way they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that. It isn't really hard to come up with various replacements if one tries at all. But again, for as rare as it is to come up, it is easy enough to not bother with Thrall and it have zero impact on a given chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:44:20-07:00","id":981132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=980904#post980904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does a cannibalism scene involving the victimization of a friend contribute? What does a murder scene involving the victimization of a friend contribute? If you think that it is that sensitive of a subject, fade to black (I would really suggest fading to black during any Thrall moment anyway) and, when the frenzy ends, have the character coming to beside the abused body (or corpse) of their victim. The PC and the ST are explicitly wanting to deal with the Thrall of the Wyrm when they choose to make a character with Rage 6+, it is not an esoteric rule because it is in the Core (Revised), so it is their responsibility for making (or allowing) a character that would fall to the Thrall of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> For an alternative Thrall to make sense, it would have to be as horrific as the other forms of Thrall. The Thrall of the Wyrm focuses on the three major taboos of Western society (Homid=Cannibalism, Metis=Rape, and Lupus=Murder). The question for the creation of an alternate Thrall rule is what would be an appropriate replacement taboo (the incest taboo is covered with the creation of the Metis and would not be appropriate for a frenzy situation anyway). I really cannot imagine an appropriate taboo that would replace the rape taboo associated with the Metis Thrall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I don't think they contribute much at all, though murder of a friend in the fit of corruptive rage is the most thematically appropriate of the three. But here's what makes the sexual assault one fundamentally distinct from those two. It is a safe bet your players have not been murdered or cannibalized. We may assume this because they are alive, and we may also assume that if they have a negative history with violence, they feel personally able to handle the violence inherent in the setting if they made an informed decision to play Werewolf. The violence is up front and unmissable. It is not such a safe bet your players have not been the subject of a sexual assault, or have in some way some baggage, trauma, or issues surrounding it. Those that do may or may not be able to confront the issue in a tabletop game (indeed, I think there may be potentially great therapeutic uses of triggering content in the hopefully safe and comforting environment of a tabletop game), and as the rule is a single rule tucked away in a long rulebook, they are less likely to have made an informed decision that 'this may be an issue'.<br /> <br /> Further, I don't think it <i>should</i> be an issue at all. While I have no objection to including sexual assault in stories and, yes, even in tabletop games, it is a subject matter that needs to be handled carefully and deliberately. 'Roll the dice. You fail. Now you have to rape someone.' is not careful and deliberate. What it is is crass, vulgar, and offensive, and for no actual gain.<br /> <br /> For alternative Thrall states, let's look for a moment at the nature of the Defiler Wyrm. It is the force behind suicide, self-mutiliation, and self-destruction of all types. It is actually more appropriate for the result of a Thrall state in a Metis to take such a form than it is for it to take on the form of a mandatory sexual assault. It's plenty 'dark' if there's a realistic chance that in any fight, the Metis berserker might claw his own eyes from his head or tear out his own tongue with all the fury in the world. Suicide and self-harm rest as taboos either on, or just below, the same tier as those of rape, murder, and cannibalism. In some cultures, they can actually sit higher for religious reasons.<br /> <br /> So, again. What does mandatory, random chance sexual assault offer that competing options can't? And just as importantly, is there more utility created by it than by a competing option that does not hinge on mandatory, random chance sexual assault scenes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T20:08:09-07:00","id":981230,"title":"","content":"So forcing a character to commit suicide is a better option (mutilation is a relatively meaningless concept to a Garou)? And when would it trigger? When they witnessed a dead or incapacitate foe? Friend? Opponent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T20:12:54-07:00","id":981233,"title":"","content":"It is a less repugnant option than a mandatory, dice-based sexual assault scene, yes. When it triggers? Whenever the Thrall state triggers.<br /> <br /> Why are you so attached to a mechanic that requires groups to play out rape due to the roll of a die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:02:55-07:00","id":981303,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981233#post981233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you so attached to a mechanic that requires groups to play out rape due to the roll of a die?</div> </div> </div> </div>Read: 'How dare you follow rules that I deem unsavory.'<br /> <br /> You want to censor your game's Metis hate-fucking? Great, I do the same; but I can see why one would like to keep that mechanic. Metis Wyrm-rides go a long way to explain why the other Garou treat them so badly; the mules aren't just the product of sin, they actively engage in in hideous behavior when they let themselves go too fully.<br /> <br /> FATAL, it ain't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-04-2016, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:13:57-07:00","id":981308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981303#post981303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Read: 'How dare you follow rules that I deem unsavory.'<br /> <br /> You want to censor your game's Metis hate-fucking? Great, I do the same; but I can see why one would like to keep that mechanic. Metis Wyrm-rides go a long way to explain why the other Garou treat them so badly; the mules aren't just the product of sin, they actively engage in in hideous behavior when they let themselves go too fully.<br /> <br /> FATAL, it ain't.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Garou engage in horrible behaviour in the thrall of the Wyrm regardless of breed. What utility does a random chance sexual assault Thrall serve that an alternative one doesn't?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:29:08-07:00","id":981310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981308#post981308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All Garou engage in horrible behaviour in the thrall of the Wyrm regardless of breed. What utility does a random chance sexual assault Thrall serve that an alternative one doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you are just being obtuse. The whole reason we are having this thread is because rape/sexual violence is often regarded as more lastingly traumatic/more evil than regular violence. This is true in game and out of game. There is a stigma attached to rapists, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> The<i> especially </i>terrible Wyrm-rides of the acursed Garou are a compelling reason for Metis to be hated/feared. That is the utility. Killing is one thing, but twisted perversion is another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:29:46-07:00","id":981311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981303#post981303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Read: 'How dare you follow rules that I deem unsavory.'<br /> <br /> You want to censor your game's Metis hate-fucking? Great, I do the same; but I can see why one would like to keep that mechanic. Metis Wyrm-rides go a long way to explain why the other Garou treat them so badly; the mules aren't just the product of sin, they actively engage in in hideous behavior when they let themselves go too fully.<br /> <br /> FATAL, it ain't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves don't like metis because their deformities remind them of the impurity of an act any one of them could commit, and are often tempted to commit. It has nothing to do with a curse that afflicts everyone and only rears its head in the rarest and most dire of circumstances. Any werewolf is gonna understand that it's not the werewolf doing that, it's the Wyrm. The feelings of violation are enough that many simply kill themselves after experiencing it. If it were common, werewolves would be constantly killing themselves.<br /> <br /> The thing is, you want to defend a mechanic? That's great, but the person you're defending was actively advocating for it, which requires a bit more of a defense than 'because it's in the book'. The discussion was &quot;Hey, I know this thing is in the book, but my players are deciding they aren't comfortable with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you rally to that talking point with 'There's nothing wrong with it,' then I put it to you that it is on that person to explain what value there is in a randomly generated rape stat, 'cause to my mind the only reason the writers could possibly have to put it there over something else, is to basically just make the game more edgy. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.riotamot.com/vampire/comic/233GeekPsyc.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.riotamot.com/vampire/comic/233GeekPsyc.jpg</a> like this, basically. <br /> <br /> And I'm aware that both of those are strawmen, but it's also a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:32:34-07:00","id":981313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981310#post981310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you are just being obtuse. The whole reason we are having this thread is because rape/sexual violence is often regarded as more lastingly traumatic/more evil than regular violence. This is true in game and out of game. There is a stigma attached to rapists, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> The<i> especially </i>terrible Wyrm-rides of the acursed Garou are a compelling reason for Metis to be hated/feared. That is the utility. Killing is one thing, but twisted perversion is another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you think being eaten while you're still alive isn't as traumatic as rape, I don't know what to say. The fact is that there are good ways to portray rape, and there are poor or 'silly' ways to portray it. Tossing rape in for a cheap emotional shock is not good writing, it's actually very poor writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T00:50:39-07:00","id":981323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981310#post981310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you are just being obtuse. The whole reason we are having this thread is because rape/sexual violence is often regarded as more lastingly traumatic/more evil than regular violence. This is true in game and out of game. There is a stigma attached to rapists, and rightly so.<br /> <br /> The<i> especially </i>terrible Wyrm-rides of the acursed Garou are a compelling reason for Metis to be hated/feared. That is the utility. Killing is one thing, but twisted perversion is another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and it is also significantly more likely to be genuinely uncomfortable - and not in a good way - for the players. Your utility is accomplished just as readily by alternative Thrall states, whether suicidal violence, the birth of a bane with intimate knowledge of that Metis's sept (hey look ma, it's a defiler bane <i>and</i> a violation of the Litany!), or even just using both other thrall states at the same time for the Metis.<br /> <br /> There's a time and a place for rape as a topic in roleplaying games. Sometimes it's never at a given table, sometimes it is. But I'm going to say that it shouldn't be down to random chance based on a core rule in the game. It should be something considered carefully by those involved, because as subject matter goes it is potentially very hurtful to an unfortunately very large number of people.<br /> <br /> When the only serious arguments for it to stay are 'it's bad, and therefore will make the PCs look bad' or 'it's bad, and therefore will make the players less comfortable' (and worse, 'it will punish munchkins'), then it lacks in relative utility. The criteria for utility I outlined earlier are simple, but they bear repeating. When you introduce something to a game, you should always be asking yourself 'How will this addition give real utility (that is, will it add value) to the game? Will it help mechanically? Will it help thematically? Most importantly, will it help the people who actually play this game create better stories? How does that stack up against the negatives of this addition?'<br /> <br /> Most of the time, it's easy. The only negatives might be say, 'system bloat' or 'do we really need another splat that does &lt;x&gt;, or 'it's violent, but in a game based around violence'. But when we start talking sexual assault, child abuse, or other massively sensitive subjects, it's harder. I put it to you that a system that, on random chance, results in PCs raping enemies or each other does not outweigh the negative aspects of the sensitive nature of the subject, the potential to cause sincere and undesirable discomfort to players, and the ability of it to hijack narratives and character direction in a way that is not met by the other Thrall states.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T06:55:13-07:00","id":981415,"title":"","content":"I am not advocating for the Metis Thrall, I am just saying that there is not a good replacement for it thematically. The Metis are supposed to be twisted, body and soul, and they are cursed by Gaia from the moment of their conception. The Metis are not disabled people who just wear fur.<br /> <br /> If you do not want to deal with it, either forbid characters from reaching Rage 6+ or remove the Thrall from your games. If you really want to replace the Metis Thrall though, you need to have something as horrific as stopping to eat the testicles (or breasts) of your still living opponent while your allies are being destroyed by your enemies. Cannibalism should be horrific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:38:44-07:00","id":981464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981415#post981415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not advocating for the Metis Thrall, I am just saying that there is not a good replacement for it thematically. The Metis are supposed to be twisted, body and soul, and they are cursed by Gaia from the moment of their conception. The Metis are not disabled people who just wear fur.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... the fact that they have one deformity that they can't get rid of somehow isn't enough on that front?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you do not want to deal with it, either forbid characters from reaching Rage 6+ or remove the Thrall from your games. If you really want to replace the Metis Thrall though, you need to have something as horrific as stopping to eat the testicles (or breasts) of your still living opponent while your allies are being destroyed by your enemies. Cannibalism should be horrific. </div> </div> </div>Or they could change the game. It's not like Thrall is an essential part of the game that's been there since day one; it was first introduced in 2e, so it could find itself out as easily as making stepping sideways not require a mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:03:21-07:00","id":981538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981415#post981415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not advocating for the Metis Thrall, I am just saying that there is not a good replacement for it thematically. The Metis are supposed to be twisted, body and soul, and they are cursed by Gaia from the moment of their conception. The Metis are not disabled people who just wear fur.<br /> <br /> If you do not want to deal with it, either forbid characters from reaching Rage 6+ or remove the Thrall from your games. If you really want to replace the Metis Thrall though, you need to have something as horrific as stopping to eat the testicles (or breasts) of your still living opponent while your allies are being destroyed by your enemies. Cannibalism should be horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>So horror isn't horror unless it's grossly sexualized? <br /> <br /> You've still yet to explain how twisting someone's soul and body into a parody of lycanthropy is less corrupted and well, <i>twisted.</i> You're just making assertions without really providing an argument for why your point of view is right, and that's not really helpful if I'm going to decide on a position for myself.<br /> <br /> For the record, I'm on the fence leaning toward not using my idea and just scrapping Thrall in general the way Forsaken did. It hasn't been because of your arguments, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:24:19-07:00","id":981553,"title":"","content":"So ignoring the argument of whether or not the RAW Metis Thrall system is necessary because it makes zero difference to the OP premise.<br /> <br /> Various options mentioned (keep in mind, I didn't go back through the whole thread, so this is purely from memory):<br /> <br /> 1) Ignore Thrall completely<br /> 2) the victim suffers a parody of lycanthropy that the Metis will have to clean up/address<br /> 3) a combination of the homid/lupus Thralls: brutalization and cannibalism<br /> 4) torture/extreme sadism (presumably without the intent to kill)<br /> 5) self mutilation (possibly suicidal)<br /> <br /> So that's at least 5 alternate options. I would favor 1 or 5 personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:16:15-07:00","id":981688,"title":"","content":"I like ignoring Thrall completely. Haven't seen a convincing argument that it serves a purpose.<br /> <br /> Also, using thrall as the reason metis are not trusted or liked and sometimes hated completely changes the theme behind what metis are and represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:41:21-07:00","id":981740,"title":"","content":"They represent perversion (incest) and corruption of body and soul. They are not disabled people in fur coats, they are representations of their parents' rejection of Garou Kinfolk. Heck, Gaia was generous enough to give Garou Kinfolk of two species, so the parents of Metis rejected the blessings of Gaia twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:49:52-07:00","id":981748,"title":"","content":"The point being that metis are not at fault for being metis and your interpretation makes them responsible for the poor treatment they receive. This is directly contrary to all of the material about metis in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> You're entitled to your own take but you're not entitled to everyone else's take, despite your arguments iin this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:14:49-07:00","id":981768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981415#post981415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not advocating for the Metis Thrall, I am just saying that there is not a good replacement for it thematically. The Metis are supposed to be twisted, body and soul, and they are cursed by Gaia from the moment of their conception. The Metis are not disabled people who just wear fur.<br /> <br /> If you do not want to deal with it, either forbid characters from reaching Rage 6+ or remove the Thrall from your games. If you really want to replace the Metis Thrall though, you need to have something as horrific as stopping to eat the testicles (or breasts) of your still living opponent while your allies are being destroyed by your enemies. Cannibalism should be horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are numerous options for it, advanced by myself and by others. To be clear, I do not object to the concept of the Thrall. I <i>do</i> object to turning rape into a 'you lost a dice roll' issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:26:02-07:00","id":981777,"title":"","content":"No, it is an issue of having Rage 6+. The PC (or the ST) choose (or allowed) to have a character of Rage 6+. If they did not want to deal with the Thrall, they could just have not created (or allowed) a character with Rage 6+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:30:32-07:00","id":981781,"title":"","content":"Or, the rule could not require rape in favour of an alternative Thrall state. Again, I'm not opposed to the concept of Thrall. I am opposed to that <i>specific</i> form of Thrall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:26:27-07:00","id":981819,"title":"","content":"The only detail of Thrall that might need to stick around is the uncontrollable nature of the frenzy, as it goes off and Willpower can't stop it. Having to go berserk or run away, no chance to resist, is plenty bad enough on its own when you're ripping and tearing anything that gets in your way.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, it's possibly to reach Thrall-success thresholds before Rage 6. You roll the greater of your temporary or permanent rating, and stimulants like cocaine or crystal meth, if taken in breed form, also make you frenzy with one less success. Then there's also the questionable decision of getting the &quot;merit&quot; Mars Midsky, which knocks two off the necessary threshold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T17:41:34-07:00","id":981832,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Mars Midsky is a rather insane choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:33:13-07:00","id":981909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981832#post981832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Mars Midsky is a rather insane choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the amount of points you spend on it, it really shouldn't be. None of the other Midsky aspects cut nearly as deeply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:38:09-07:00","id":981913,"title":"","content":"WW always had a problem with properly balancing Merits and Flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:04:57-07:00","id":981942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=981913#post981913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WW always had a problem with properly balancing Merits and Flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we should stop there because...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:30:01-07:00","id":981949,"title":"","content":"I am not disagreeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:44:40-07:00","id":982014,"title":"","content":"just another little bit that could possibly play into it: there are other things that can easily increase your temporary rage above 6.<br /> It only came to mind because I play in a game where this happens regularly as we ended up with Bear as our Totem which, every time a pack-mate gets their first wound in combat, gives the rest of the pack +2 temporary rage.<br /> In our case we have a pack of 6 characters so that could potentially mean +10 rage for everyone in a given battle. Of course oftentimes someone will have other things to do during a fight or some members will not get hurt for whatever reason but +6 rage is not out of the question at all...<br /> <br /> Also I think there are fetishes and other stuff that give you a certain amount of additional temporary rage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:37:37-07:00","id":982077,"title":"","content":"I'm going to start with the initial question being begged by several here: &quot;What's the point of Thralls?&quot;<br /> <br /> I imagine I'm starting to sound like a broken record on this, but I'll remind as always- The 'Darkness' in the World of Darkness has lightened up a lot over the editions. What we play today is a modified version of a thematically different game. So the argument that Thrall doesn't belong in W20 and to a lesser extent Revised might be a valid one.<br /> <br /> Here's my grasp of the idea behind Thrall and Frenzy: It's about being a monster. The characters are monsters. That is a pretty big deal. There's a reason they Fera aren't all buddy teammates working together against the Wyrm and introducing themselves to mankind to lead them into salvation. They are MONSTERS. The Curse isn't just some annoying mechanic, the rage vs. willpower unbalancing isn't simply an anti-munchkin system, and Thrall isn't meant just to discourage high Rage. It's all to drive home that Garou are monsters, fueled by Rage no human can or will EVER truly understand (which should be haunting enough, given what mundane rage IS capable of), and harboring a beast they honestly can't control. That beast getting out and having to live with the unbearable shame and guilt is a defining part of Garou existence. How many kinfolk do you think have died by their hands? When sex, anger, frustration, insult and injury can all call for Rage rolls? Do you think it's a coincidence that some Garou might choose to treat them as insignificant.... perhaps as a coping mechanism?<br /> <br /> So there's your theme. Garou are supposed to be, at least on some level, afraid of and ashamed of themselves. Between the Impergium, two War of Rages, utter failure at their duty, and a history of being abusers... they're second only to the Weaver in culpability for the Apocalypse, and I'm still not tracking a way for them to fix any of this sitting around, waiting to be claimed. Thematically, Thrall is the personal-level shame meant to mirror the shame the Garou Race is meant to harbor as a whole.<br /> <br /> If you and/or any of your players don't want that level of Darkness in your World of Darkness, that's what the Golden Rule is for, and why this thread is a good idea. But that doesn't mean other groups should be condemned for playing as-written. You might be surprised how many players find catharsis in killing members of that Fomori breed that propagates through rape, dismantling Pentex-run 'Pray the Gay Away' straight-camps, re-confronting an old personal trauma from a position of (supernatural) power, or perhaps even forgiving a character who wronged theirs and moving beyond it. You do you; let them do them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm#post980034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This in mind, I've come up with a replacement Thrall of the Wyrm result whenever it comes up for Metis. I wanted to present this here in case it's too 'out there'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of what you're going for... namely a way to provide an alternative for groups who are sensitive to the subject. My take is that this meets half of what Thrall is going for. It checks the box that it leaves the Metis with powerful guilt (assuming they aren't a cold-hearted bastard), but in my opinion the supernatural aspect almost feels like it lessens their hand in the matter. Like, they're the means by which the corruption gets to the victim... but Garou generally don't have the power to curse people without a few rare gifts/rites, so it sort of feels like it's more directly the Wyrm's fault rather than once-removed.<br /> <br /> I do like the previous suggestions of mutilating the bodies (like Reavers from Firefly, for example... though again, without the Rape if that's your preferred variant). It keeps the misdeed directly in the hands of the Metis, but removes the unwanted element.<br /> <br /> Of course, again, it's your game and your call. I don't dislike what's written for any reason other than the above... and in a sense it would add another level of disfavor for Metis as they become a liability to the Veil for yet another reason. That is pretty thematically solid, there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:44:37-07:00","id":982080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=982077#post982077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to start with the initial question being begged by several here: &quot;What's the point of Thralls?&quot;<br /> <br /> I imagine I'm starting to sound like a broken record on this, but I'll remind as always- The 'Darkness' in the World of Darkness has lightened up a lot over the editions. What we play today is a modified version of a thematically different game. So the argument that Thrall doesn't belong in W20 and to a lesser extent Revised might be a valid one.<br /> <br /> Here's my grasp of the idea behind Thrall and Frenzy: It's about being a monster. The characters are monsters. That is a pretty big deal. There's a reason they Fera aren't all buddy teammates working together against the Wyrm and introducing themselves to mankind to lead them into salvation. They are MONSTERS. The Curse isn't just some annoying mechanic, the rage vs. willpower unbalancing isn't simply an anti-munchkin system, and Thrall isn't meant just to discourage high Rage. It's all to drive home that Garou are monsters, fueled by Rage no human can or will EVER truly understand (which should be haunting enough, given what mundane rage IS capable of), and harboring a beast they honestly can't control. That beast getting out and having to live with the unbearable shame and guilt is a defining part of Garou existence. How many kinfolk do you think have died by their hands? When sex, anger, frustration, insult and injury can all call for Rage rolls? Do you think it's a coincidence that some Garou might choose to treat them as insignificant.... perhaps as a coping mechanism?<br /> <br /> So there's your theme. Garou are supposed to be, at least on some level, afraid of and ashamed of themselves. Between the Impergium, two War of Rages, utter failure at their duty, and a history of being abusers... they're second only to the Weaver in culpability for the Apocalypse, and I'm still not tracking a way for them to fix any of this sitting around, waiting to be claimed. Thematically, Thrall is the personal-level shame meant to mirror the shame the Garou Race is meant to harbor as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll ask you the same question I've asked everyone else. What utility does the Metis Thrall, as it is currently written, add that an alternative Thrall state cannot also add?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you and/or any of your players don't want that level of Darkness in your World of Darkness, that's what the Golden Rule is for, and why this thread is a good idea. But that doesn't mean other groups should be condemned for playing as-written. You might be surprised how many players find catharsis in killing members of that Fomori breed that propagates through rape, dismantling Pentex-run 'Pray the Gay Away' straight-camps, re-confronting an old personal trauma from a position of (supernatural) power, or perhaps even forgiving a character who wronged theirs and moving beyond it. You do you; let them do them. </div> </div> </div>Shockingly, no one here has said other people can't play the game as they like or that it can be cathartic or emotionally healthy and helpful to confront these issues. I've been the loudest critic of the rape Thrall so far, and I've also been the one saying that rape has a time and place as a subject matter - and that that time and place is different for different groups, based on their specific experiences and goals for the game. You're arguing against a strawman here.<br /> <br /> What <i>has</i> been said is that reducing rape to the status of 'you rolled poorly, now it's rape time' is not okay and that it shouldn't be present as a core rule in a game not specifically centred around themes of sexual violence (if at all). Do you think it is or should be? I'd like to hear your reasons, if you do.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:22:58-07:00","id":982133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=982077#post982077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to start with the initial question being begged by several here: &quot;What's the point of Thralls?&quot;<br /> <br /> I imagine I'm starting to sound like a broken record on this, but I'll remind as always- The 'Darkness' in the World of Darkness has lightened up a lot over the editions. What we play today is a modified version of a thematically different game. So the argument that Thrall doesn't belong in W20 and to a lesser extent Revised might be a valid one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counter-point: 1e was arguably the darkest version of the game, and didn't have Thrall anywhere in it. TotW was added in 2e, and it feels as extraneous as tribal weaknesses, also a later addition to the game*. There are, again I emphasize, parts I could think of keeping, but the name and additional roll-to-avoid effects need to go. Garou will still be monstrous, even if Rage doesn't come from the Wyrm (and judging from the fact that Weaver and Wyld spirits have it, it probably doesn't) and they don't sexually assault victims in the throes of said frenzy, instead just attacking and killing the vague, red-tinged shapes that they see set before them.<br /> <br /> * When randomly lashing out, I blame a desire to force symmetry with Vampire for both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:15:10-07:00","id":982255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=982077#post982077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to start with the initial question being begged by several here: &quot;What's the point of Thralls?&quot;<br /> <br /> I like the idea of what you're going for... namely a way to provide an alternative for groups who are sensitive to the subject. My take is that this meets half of what Thrall is going for. It checks the box that it leaves the Metis with powerful guilt (assuming they aren't a cold-hearted bastard), but in my opinion the supernatural aspect almost feels like it lessens their hand in the matter. Like, they're the means by which the corruption gets to the victim... but Garou generally don't have the power to curse people without a few rare gifts/rites, so it sort of feels like it's more directly the Wyrm's fault rather than once-removed.<br /> <br /> I do like the previous suggestions of mutilating the bodies (like Reavers from Firefly, for example... though again, without the Rape if that's your preferred variant). It keeps the misdeed directly in the hands of the Metis, but removes the unwanted element.<br /> <br /> Of course, again, it's your game and your call. I don't dislike what's written for any reason other than the above... and in a sense it would add another level of disfavor for Metis as they become a liability to the Veil for yet another reason. That is pretty thematically solid, there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible I didn't word it well. It's not meant to 'lessen' their hand. The Defiler Wyrm shares that trait with them briefly, and then through their bite they infect the other person, because they <i>want</i> it. They want what everyone else gets to have but they never will.<br /> <br /> That aside, the only reason any of the Thralls work is because the Wyrm takes hold of them, they are not in control of their actions at that point, so doesn't the Thrall lessen their hand in general?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:12:25-07:00","id":982425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=982255#post982255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's possible I didn't word it well. It's not meant to 'lessen' their hand. The Defiler Wyrm shares that trait with them briefly, and then through their bite they infect the other person, because they <i>want</i> it. They want what everyone else gets to have but they never will.<br /> <br /> That aside, the only reason any of the Thralls work is because the Wyrm takes hold of them, they are not in control of their actions at that point, so doesn't the Thrall lessen their hand in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, totally. I didn't mean to imply you were trying to. But looking at it from the horror and shame perspective, which is more horrifying a guilt-wracking: someone with the touch of Midas that accidentally turns your arm to gold... or someone being mind-controlled and sawing your arm off with their own two hands and a rusty hacksaw?<br /> <br /> Either way you're out an arm, right?<br /> <br /> I think the supernatural effect, as compared to a more physical, body-on-body attack, makes it psychologically easier for the victim (and transgressor) to differentiate blame on a sub-conscious level (even if there's no change on the conscious level... either way the person didn't have a say in their own actions). It's less about the level of the guilt and more about the flavor, for me. I admit it's pretty darn nit-picky.<br /> <br /> As for Saur Ops's point, I would argue that the darkest the setting got was probably early-2e, with the bell-curve of horror both rising and falling again during the 2e run. Don't forget that's actually when a lot of the Black Dog material came out, and also when the gamelines started their seemingly endless big dick contest where it looked like the actual line authors were trying to settle the &quot;Which splat would win?&quot; debate by releasing progressively more asinine additions to their games (True Brujah, anyone?).<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I know what the intent of Thrall was, though. Maybe the authors felt Frenzy for Garou wasn't &quot;Frenzied&quot; enough or it was getting mechanically sidestepped, or with so many berserker PC-types it was being seen more as a power than a liability (&quot;No wound penalties! Wooo!&quot;). I can only make my own guesses based on the assumption of good intentions. Then again, I also thought Ginsberg was really deep until I read his journals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T18:46:27-07:00","id":982483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=982425#post982425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Saur Ops's point, I would argue that the darkest the setting got was probably early-2e, with the bell-curve of horror both rising and falling again during the 2e run. Don't forget that's actually when a lot of the Black Dog material came out, and also when the gamelines started their seemingly endless big dick contest where it looked like the actual line authors were trying to settle the &quot;Which splat would win?&quot; debate by releasing progressively more asinine additions to their games (True Brujah, anyone?).<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean I know what the intent of Thrall was, though. Maybe the authors felt Frenzy for Garou wasn't &quot;Frenzied&quot; enough or it was getting mechanically sidestepped, or with so many berserker PC-types it was being seen more as a power than a liability (&quot;No wound penalties! Wooo!&quot;). I can only make my own guesses based on the assumption of good intentions. Then again, I also thought Ginsberg was really deep until I read his journals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was BDGF material dark, or was it just kind of... there? The essay on werewolves as bad guys in the 1e player's guide seems way darker than Freak Legion and its random powers and taints table.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Trujah and other DSotBH material, I'd heard (admittedly from some random edit on TV tropes) that it was part of the writer making as big a mess as possible before parting ways with WW. Also, a lot of the most broken Disciplines were arguably in the core... like the old version of Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T03:19:07-07:00","id":982624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=982483#post982483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was BDGF material dark, or was it just kind of... there? The essay on werewolves as bad guys in the 1e player's guide seems way darker than Freak Legion and its random powers and taints table.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience is that Freak Legion is mostly used so you can stat up your ex as a Fomor and watch the PCs tear her to pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:31:06-07:00","id":982660,"title":"","content":"Really? Never did that myself. I ended up using Freakfeet in NYC as a form of malevolent sapient rat though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:49:04-07:00","id":982718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=982624#post982624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience is that Freak Legion is mostly used so you can stat up your ex as a Fomor and watch the PCs tear her to pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Puts sunglasses on at night]<br /> <br /> So dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:50:25-07:00","id":983147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=982624#post982624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience is that Freak Legion is mostly used so you can stat up your ex as a Fomor and watch the PCs tear her to pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or co-workers that piss you off* Whistles innocently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T02:38:31-07:00","id":983228,"title":"","content":"I actually prefer using Possessed instead of Freak Legion. The fomori created with Possessed gain five free Power Points and can sacrifice two levels of permanent Autonomy without becoming too inhuman, giving them a fifteen Power Point advantage over Freak Legion fomori. Mages especially hate running into fomori created under Possessed rules because they usually do not detect anything wrong before they are attacked. Homogeneity sucks for Mages, since they do not have any innate powers to help them when their Spheres fail them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:03:20-07:00","id":983520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980034-metis-and-the-defiler-wyrm?p=983228#post983228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually prefer using Possessed instead of Freak Legion. The fomori created with Possessed gain five free Power Points and can sacrifice two levels of permanent Autonomy without becoming too inhuman, giving them a fifteen Power Point advantage over Freak Legion fomori. Mages especially hate running into fomori created under Possessed rules because they usually do not detect anything wrong before they are attacked. Homogeneity sucks for Mages, since they do not have any innate powers to help them when their Spheres fail them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a player character, I generally agree... but honestly, the mechanics in Possessed can allow for some incredible, dare I say &quot;Garou-crushing&quot;, builds for a starting Fomor. I generally reserve the creation rules in Possessed for the elites and story signature characters, and stick with 2-3 power archetypes for the shock troops of the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:13:38-07:00","id":983525,"title":"","content":"Well, I am not quite sure that a Fomori with Autonomy 7 could be 'Garou-crushing', though a Fomori with Autonomy 5 could be 'Garou-crushing', but I see your point. An Autonomy 7 Fomori would definitely be 'Mage-crushing' though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T05:36:55-07:00","id":983863,"title":"","content":"N.B. One Fomor, Two Fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}